# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# .dockerignore does NOT inherit .gitignore — Docker sends everything in this
# directory to the daemon unless it is listed here, including files git never
# tracked. Without this file the context is ~611 MB, almost all of it the two
# dependency trees; with it, ~2 MB.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependency trees — reinstalled inside the image from the lockfiles.
# Copying them in would also ship host-built native binaries (@swc/core is
# pinned to an exact version and resolves per-platform), which is precisely
# the class of breakage T4.1 avoids by building on Debian.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
web/node_modules

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output — all of it is regenerated inside the image.
#
# public/ matters most: it is the Angular bundle. Sending the host's copy
# risks the exact failure T2.1 fixed — an image serving whichever main-*.js
# happened to be lying around rather than the one the image built.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build
public
web/dist
web/.angular
tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. .env holds APP_KEY, the database password and SMTP credentials, and
# must never enter an image layer — layers persist even if a later step deletes
# the file. Production config is supplied at runtime instead (T6.3).
# .env.example is deliberately kept: it is a template with no real values.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.docker
.env.local
.env.production.local
.env.development.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control and tooling metadata.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.claude
.editorconfig
.vscode
.idea
.fleet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and source data. The competency workbooks are imported into
# Postgres, never read by the running app, and are large; keep them out even
# though the root is currently clean of them (see T7.1, which loads more).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs
*.md
!README.md
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs, dumps and OS noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backups
*.log
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
*.dump
*.sql
.DS_Store

# NOTE: tests/ is deliberately NOT excluded. `node ace build` compiles it as
# part of the TypeScript project, and the suite is two small spec files.
